// Go Fish — 3 players, ask the next player for a rank you hold, lay down
// books (sets of four).
//
// Rules:
//   - 52-card deck; each player is dealt 7 cards.
//   - On your turn, ask the next player for one rank **that you hold**: if
//     they hold any cards of that rank, they must hand them over; otherwise
//     you draw one card from the deck (go fish). Ranks you do not hold are
//     not offered (standard rule).
//   - After the ask, you may lay down a book: four cards of the same rank.
//     The engine validates the chosen set against the `Book` combo (submit
//     0 cards to skip). Books land on your Books pile and score 4 points.
//   - The game ends when the deck runs out or a player empties their hand
//     (or after 24 turns); the most books wins.
//
// Remaining deviations from standard Go Fish (engine-gated, not authoring):
//   - You may only ask the *next* player (standard: any player) — the
//     engine has no "choose a player as move source" prompt.
//   - A successful ask does not grant another ask — the engine has no
//     conditional re-ask loop inside a turn.
//
// Engine notes:
//   - The ask is a 13-way `choose` (one option per rank); each option is
//     guarded by `"<Rank>" in Hand of current` so unheld ranks are no-ops.
//   - `Hand where Rank is "X" of next` combines a where-filter with an
//     owner; the engine resolves the base location against the owner
//     ("next"), not the current player.
//   - Each ask option checks the emptiness *first* and deals *after*: on a
//     hit the transfer happens and no draw occurs; on a miss the draw
//     happens and the (empty) transfer is a no-op. (Order matters — caught
//     by the behavioral fixtures.)
//   - Laying down uses the combo-source move (`ComboSource`): the player
//     picks cards from the whole hand and the engine validates them against
//     the combo filter, re-prompting on mismatch. `same Rank` matches any
//     duplicated rank, so a 2+2 split also passes the filter — a documented
//     simplification of the combo semantics (engine-vs-design.md D-16). The
//     guard only prompts when duplicated ranks exist; 0 cards skips.
//   - Scoring is by books (4 points per book) instead of hand size.

player P1, P2, P3
turnorder (P:P1, P:P2, P:P3)
location Hand on all
location Books on all
location Deck on table

combo Book where (same Rank and size >= 4)

card on Deck:
  Rank(Ace, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven, Eight, Nine, Ten, Jack, Queen, King)
    for Suit(Diamonds, Clubs, Hearts, Spades)

shuffle Deck

stage Deal for current 1 times {
  deal 7 from Deck private to Hand of all
}

stage Ask for current until (Deck empty or Hand of current empty) or 24 times {
  choose {
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Ace" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Ace" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Two" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Two" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Three" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Three" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Four" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Four" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Five" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Five" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Six" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Six" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Seven" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Seven" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Eight" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Eight" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Nine" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Nine" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Ten" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Ten" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Jack" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Jack" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "Queen" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "Queen" of next private to Hand of current
    or
    if (size(cards Hand where Rank is "King" of next) == 0) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    deal Hand where Rank is "King" of next private to Hand of current
  }
  if (not Book in Hand of current empty) {
    optional {
      move Book in Hand of current private to Books
    }
  }
  cycle to next
}

stage Score for current 3 times {
  score size(cards Books of current) to current
  cycle to next
}

stage End for current 1 times {
  winner is highest score
}
